 "provenance": "Tibet 1 (world 2, level 0) normal exit 51,9, control-only from spawn on the exact S700 core (logic and paint each frame). Start values: weaponTier 2 (choosing Tibet on the seal grants tier >= 2, cGame.method_75), maxHealth 4 (no armor needed), lives 12 (campaign value used by the other Tibet routes), redDiamonds 25 (the Tibet seal price; it has no effect inside this stage), diamonds 0. No damage, no deaths, no resets; 2240 ticks. Route: red-diamond chest 2,2; upper trap corridor; checkpoint 34,4; hidden spiral to the 75-diamond chest 53,5 (the 35-diamond magic lock 50,9 is then satisfied); the four diagonal ceiling traps by the exit gate (44,8 43,9 42,10 41,11) triggered one by one and dodged; ice bricks of the two-row corridor 32-40 x 8-9 broken with the hammer, the two freed turtles (enemy 49) dodged, checkpoint 31,8; down the grass/stone column, two ceiling traps triggered and dodged, checkpoint 36,16, gold-key chest 38,14 opened; back up the column (a stone pushed into the 31,9 pocket) to 30,8. Turtles: they bounce between x=32 and x=40 on rows 8 and 9 (cGame.method_325) and are only updated within 8 cells of the hero (method_304), so both were parked at x=40, blocking the corridor exit 40,9->40,10. The hero steps into 32,8 to wake them, then back to 31,8 after the row-9 turtle has left x=40 but before the row-8 turtle does, so the row-8 turtle freezes again at 40 while the row-9 turtle keeps walking west. After 28 ticks the hero runs east on row 8 (waking the row-8 turtle), lets the row-9 turtle pass below, drops to 35,9 behind it and runs to 40,9, 40,10, 40,11 while the row-8 turtle passes above. Then 47,8: the gold key opens lock 48,8 and gate 48,9; through the gate and the magic lock to the exit 51,9.",
